# Build outputs — rebuilt inside the image
**/build/
.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/test-results/

# Installed dependencies (every stage runs its own `npm ci` / Gradle resolve). Recursive so a nested
# workspace can never leak a host-built node_modules (native binaries) into a COPY.
**/node_modules/

# Agent/tooling state: skills, docs, settings and — in a primary checkout — every git worktree
# under .claude/worktrees/ (each with its own node_modules/build). Measured on the primary
# checkout: the context transfer fell from 3.84 GB to 17.7 MB. No Dockerfile stage reads .claude/.
.claude/

# The deterministic sample plan (loaded into a DEVELOPMENT stack through the API by scripts/sample-plan/load.mjs) and the Jira stub dataset
# (sample-data/jira-stub, ~20 MB of WireMock mappings and bodies): test data, never part of the APP image. No Dockerfile stage copies them; excluding
# them here keeps a future broad COPY from shipping them. The stub has its OWN image, built with sample-data/jira-stub itself as the
# context (its Dockerfile COPYs mappings/ and __files/ from there), so this root ignore file does not apply to that build.
sample-data/

# IDE / local cruft (.git stays IN the context — the SPA build stage reads the
# commit sha/timestamp from it for the version stamp)
**/.idea/
**/*.iml
server/h2.mv.db
